<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Torrazzo of Cremona</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">completed 1309</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Torrazzo is the bell tower of Cremona Cathedral in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a>, about 112 metres tall and completed around 1309. One of the tallest medieval brick towers in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, it became the symbol of the commune. An astronomical clock was added to its face in 1583.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/torrazzo-of-cremona.jpg" alt="Torrazzo of Cremona" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: sedoglia · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cremona01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
